 { It is with great pleasure that I introduce the new 'Bonus Puzzles' chapter. I want to express my sincere appreciation for your continued support and interest in this course. Your enthusiasm for learning and improving your calculation skills motivates me to continue developing and updating this course. This chapter consists of 25 puzzles and the goal is to help you further refine the techniques that we have covered in this course. However, please note that these puzzles are not meant to substitute your regular training routine, as you need to solve thousands of puzzles to become a master. Rather, the purpose of these puzzles is to assess your ability to execute everything you have learnt in the course. Hence, as you work through these puzzles, set a goal for yourself to not only solve as many puzzles as possible but also to notice the same underlying tactical motifs that I have pointed out in the annotations. By doing so, you will train yourself to apply the techniques correctly, which will benefit you when you proceed with independent puzzle-solving outside this course. } 1. -- 
