1... { -KEY- } Qd7 { In the initial position, Black's Queen and Rook were forked. On the other hand, White had four tactical weaknesses - the unprotected e6 Knight, b5 Queen, and f1 Rook, as well as the weak back rank. Recognising that the b5 Queen is both unprotected and tied down the defence of f1, Black has this simple fork of Queen and Knight. } 2. Qe2 { White can try to save the Queen while maintaining defence on the f1 Rook. However, Black can simply get rid of their hanging Rook first, then take the e6 Knight. } ( 2. Qxd7 { White's Queen cannot abandon the Rook because of checkmate. } Rxf1 ) 
 ( 2. Rxa1 Qxb5 3. Nxf8 Kxf8 { Black has a Queen for a Rook and pawn. } ) 
Rxf1+ 3. Qxf1 Qxe6 { Black has a Rook against White's pawn. } 
