 { This is taken from a game played by WFM Maaike Keetman, VP of Content here at Chessable. } 1. { -KEY- } Bb4 $1 { The unprotected Black pieces were the d4 Knight, e7 Bishop, and h8 Rook. 1. Bb4 skewers Black's pieces, and there is no way for Black's Rook to move while defending the e7 Bishop. } axb4 { If the Bishop is taken, then we recapture on b4, threatening both the c5 Rook and the h8 Rook via the Ra8+ skewer. } 2. axb4 Rc6 3. Ra8+ Kd7 4. Rxh8 { At the end of the day, White has won a pawn and Rook for just one Bishop. } 
